Sales Insight Project
Overview
The Sales Insight Project analyzes historical sales data to uncover patterns, trends, and actionable insights that help improve decision-making in business operations.
The goal is to answer key business questions such as:
Which products and regions drive the most revenue?
How do seasonal trends affect sales?
Which customer segments are most profitable?
Where are the opportunities to optimize performance?
This project integrates data analysis, visualization, and business intelligence techniques to deliver clear insights.
Features:
Data Cleaning & Preprocessing
Handle missing data, duplicates, and inconsistencies.
Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
Identify sales trends and correlations.
Sales KPIs
Revenue, Profit, Cost, and Growth metrics.
Dashboards & Visualization
Interactive dashboards for sales trends by region, category, and time.
Predictive Insights (Optional)
Machine learning models for forecasting future sales.
Tech Stack
Visualization Tools: Power BI / Tableau / Matplotlib
Data Source: Database (MySQL / PostgreSQL)
Workflow
Data Acquisition – Collect raw sales data.
Data Preparation – Clean, transform, and enrich data.
Analysis & Insights – Perform EDA, calculate KPIs.
Dashboard Development – Build BI dashboards.
Insights Delivery – Present actionable insights to stakeholders.

Key Insights:
Top 20% of customers contribute 65% of revenue.
Q4 shows consistent seasonal spikes in sales.
Region X underperforms despite high customer volume.
How to Run
Clone this repository:
git clone https://github.com/SaitejaVinukonda/sales-insights/new/main
